{
  "uid": "sightline-agent",
  "title": "Sightline \u2014 the agent",
  "description": "What the agent answers, whether the answers hold up, and what each one costs.",
  "tags": ["sightline"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "refresh": "5m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "price_in",
        "type": "constant",
        "label": "$ per 1M input tokens",
        "query": "3",
        "current": {
          "text": "3",
          "value": "3"
        },
        "hide": 0,
        "description": "Anthropic's input price for the configured model. Sonnet is 3."
      },
      {
        "name": "price_out",
        "type": "constant",
        "label": "$ per 1M output tokens",
        "query": "15",
        "current": {
          "text": "15",
          "value": "15"
        },
        "hide": 0,
        "description": "Output price. Sonnet is 15 - five times input, which is why the money split and the token split differ."
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Is it answering, and can the answers be trusted?",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "description": "Quality before cost: an agent that answers cheaply and wrongly is worse than no agent.",
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Questions (24h)",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(sightline_agent_questions_total[24h]))"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Total asked. Every panel below is a ratio against this, so a small number here means the rest is noise rather than signal."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "title": "Unsupported citations per 100 answers",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "100 * sum(increase(sightline_agent_unsupported_citations_total[24h])) / clamp_min(sum(increase(sightline_agent_questions_total[24h])), 1)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 10
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Identifiers the agent named that no tool ever returned - the closest honest measure of hallucination this product has. Can exceed 100: one answer may invent several. Anything above zero is worth reading the answer for."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "title": "Answers that ran out of steps",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "100 * sum(increase(sightline_agent_questions_total{outcome=\"tool_limit\"}[24h])) / clamp_min(sum(increase(sightline_agent_questions_total[24h])), 1)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "percent",
          "decimals": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 5
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 20
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "The loop hit its eight-step cap and returned an apology instead of an answer. Paid for in full, eight model calls deep. A climbing number means questions are arriving that the curated tools cannot actually answer."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "Read-only notice added by the guard",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "100 * sum(increase(sightline_agent_readonly_notice_added_total[24h])) / clamp_min(sum(increase(sightline_agent_questions_total[24h])), 1)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "percent",
          "decimals": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "The prompt tells the model to say plainly that it cannot change anything; this counts the times it did not and the guard said it instead. A prompt-compliance rate, measured rather than assumed - and the reason the guarantee lives in code and not in the prompt."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "title": "Outcomes over time",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (increase(sightline_agent_questions_total[1h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "answered, unsupported_citations, tool_limit. The second and third are the interesting lines; the first is the baseline they are measured against."
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Tool results the model never saw whole (24h)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "increase(sightline_agent_truncated_results_total[24h])",
          "legendFormat": "truncated"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "A tool returned more than 12,000 characters, so the model answered from a prefix while believing it had everything. The one way a correct tool produces a wrong answer, and it is invisible in the answer itself."
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "What does it cost?",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12
      },
      "description": "Priced through the price_in / price_out variables, not hardcoded - change them when the model or the rate card changes.",
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "title": "Spend per hour, now",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(sum(rate(sightline_agent_tokens_total{kind=\"input\"}[1h])) * 3600 / 1e6 * $price_in) + (sum(rate(sightline_agent_tokens_total{kind=\"output\"}[1h])) * 3600 / 1e6 * $price_out)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "currencyUSD",
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Current burn, extrapolated from the last hour of tokens. The number to watch while somebody is demonstrating the product."
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Spend, last 24h",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 13
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(sum(increase(sightline_agent_tokens_total{kind=\"input\"}[24h])) / 1e6 * $price_in) + (sum(increase(sightline_agent_tokens_total{kind=\"output\"}[24h])) / 1e6 * $price_out)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "currencyUSD",
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "What yesterday actually cost."
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "title": "Cost per answer (24h)",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "((sum(increase(sightline_agent_tokens_total{kind=\"input\"}[24h])) / 1e6 * $price_in) + (sum(increase(sightline_agent_tokens_total{kind=\"output\"}[24h])) / 1e6 * $price_out)) / clamp_min(sum(increase(sightline_agent_questions_total[24h])), 1)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "currencyUSD",
          "decimals": 4
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "The unit economic. It rising while question volume is flat means the prompt is bloating or the model is working harder for the same answers."
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "title": "At this rate, 30 days",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 13
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "((sum(rate(sightline_agent_tokens_total{kind=\"input\"}[1h])) * 3600 / 1e6 * $price_in) + (sum(rate(sightline_agent_tokens_total{kind=\"output\"}[1h])) * 3600 / 1e6 * $price_out)) * 720"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "currencyUSD",
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "A projection, not a forecast - it assumes the last hour repeats 720 times. Useful for the order of magnitude, which is the only thing worth knowing before there is real traffic."
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "title": "Tokens per hour",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 17
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (kind) (rate(sightline_agent_tokens_total[1h])) * 3600",
          "legendFormat": "{{kind}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Input dwarfs output, because every step resends the system prompt, the seventeen tool schemas and every prior tool result."
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "title": "Where the money goes (24h)",
      "type": "piechart",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 17
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "input",
          "expr": "sum(increase(sightline_agent_tokens_total{kind=\"input\"}[24h])) / 1e6 * $price_in"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "output",
          "expr": "sum(increase(sightline_agent_tokens_total{kind=\"output\"}[24h])) / 1e6 * $price_out"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "currencyUSD"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Not the same shape as the token split: output costs several times what input does, so a thin slice of tokens can be a thick slice of the bill. This is the panel that tells you which one to optimise.",
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "values": ["value", "percent"]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "title": "Tokens per answer",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 17
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (kind) (rate(sightline_agent_tokens_total[6h])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(sightline_agent_questions_total[6h])), 0.0001)",
          "legendFormat": "{{kind}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Context cost per question. This is the prompt-bloat line: it moves when the prompt or the tool schemas grow, and not when traffic does."
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "title": "How hard is it working for each answer?",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "description": "Latency and effort. A slow answer and an expensive answer are usually the same answer.",
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "title": "Answer latency",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(sightline_agent_duration_seconds_bucket[6h])))"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(sightline_agent_duration_seconds_bucket[6h])))"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(sightline_agent_duration_seconds_bucket[6h])))"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "End to end, including every tool call, as the person waiting experiences it. p99 past thirty seconds is past where people wait."
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "title": "Latency distribution",
      "type": "heatmap",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 25
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (le) (increase(sightline_agent_duration_seconds_bucket[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{le}}",
          "format": "heatmap"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "The shape behind the percentiles. Two bands rather than one spread usually means two kinds of question - one the tools answer directly, one the model has to work at.",
      "options": {
        "calculate": false,
        "cellGap": 1,
        "color": {
          "mode": "scheme",
          "scheme": "Oranges",
          "steps": 64
        },
        "yAxis": {
          "unit": "s"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "title": "Steps per answer",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 32
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(sightline_agent_steps_bucket[6h])))"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(sightline_agent_steps_bucket[6h])))"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 1
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Model round-trips, against a cap of eight. p95 sitting at the cap means the loop is routinely running out rather than concluding - and every step is a paid call."
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "title": "Tool calls per answer",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 32
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(sightline_agent_tool_calls_total[6h])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(sightline_agent_questions_total[6h])), 0.0001)",
          "legendFormat": "calls/answer"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Evidence gathered per question. Climbing without latency climbing is the model getting thorough; climbing with it is the model flailing."
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "title": "Step distribution",
      "type": "heatmap",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 32
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (le) (increase(sightline_agent_steps_bucket[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{le}}",
          "format": "heatmap"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Where answers actually finish. Healthy work clusters at two or three; mass in the last bucket is the eight-step cap being hit.",
      "options": {
        "calculate": false,
        "cellGap": 1,
        "color": {
          "mode": "scheme",
          "scheme": "Blues",
          "steps": 64
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "title": "What is it asking the graph for?",
      "type": "row",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 39
      },
      "description": "Which evidence the model reaches for, and what it reached for and was refused.",
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "title": "Tool mix (24h)",
      "type": "bargauge",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 40
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "topk(12, sum by (tool) (increase(sightline_agent_tool_calls_total[24h])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{tool}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "Which of the curated tools earn their place. A tool absent from this list was never called at all - its schema is still being sent to the model on every single step, and paid for. The list is also the shape of the questions people actually ask.",
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "title": "Raw SQL the model was refused (24h)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 40
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "Prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "Prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (increase(sightline_agent_raw_query_refused_total[24h]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {},
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "description": "hosted means the model reached for the raw-query escape hatch that ADR-016 switches off for hosted tenants - not an attack, a sign the curated tools have a gap. The other causes come from the SQL guard: not_select is the model attempting a write, table or function a reach outside the inventory views, and execution a query Postgres failed or timed out."
    }
  ]
}
